  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Accelerating the Uptake of HIV Drug Resistance in PNG (ACT-UP-PNG 2) (Asia-Pacific)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Accelerating the Uptake of HIV Drug Resistance surveillance initiatives in Papua New Guinea (ACTUP-PNG) (2024-27) Phase 2&apos;s key program goals include that Papua New Guinea&#x2019;s public health system are strengthened to improve detection, treatment, and prevention of the communicable disease threats of HIV, syphilis, and hepatitis B, to address equity in the delivery of these functions. Additionally, Papua New Guinea has improved data and health systems capabilities to deliver equitable public health action to improve the lives of all people with HIV and prevent vertical transmission of HIV, syphilis, and hepatitis B from mothers to children. This initiative is an extension to ACT-UP PNG which commenced in 2020 with support from DFAT under the Health Security Initiative (HSI) (2017-22 - agreement 75892). See also INO390/79488.</narrative>
  </description>
